    "comments": {
      "bugs": {
        "2036045": {
          "comments": [
            {
              "attachment_id": 9575428,
              "author": "bcaliman@mozilla.com",
              "bug_id": 2036045,
              "count": 0,
              "creation_time": "2026-04-30T12:11:25Z",
              "creator": "bcaliman@mozilla.com",
              "id": 18049522,
              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "**Found in**\n* 151.0b3\n\n**Affected versions**\n* Nigthly - 152.0a1 \n* Firefox Beta - 151.0b3\n* Firefox 150.0.1\n* Firefox 140.10.1 ESR\n* Firefox 115.35.1 ESR\n\n**Tested platforms**\n* Affected platforms: macOS 26.4, Windows 11, Ubuntu 24.04\n\n**Preconditions**\n* Run this on a fresh profile\n\n**Steps to reproduce**\n1. Navigate to [AOL videos site.](https://www.aol.com/video/)\n2. Check the displayed videos.\n\n**Expected result**\n* The videos should be fully loaded (thumbnails and title as well).\n\n**Actual result**\n* The thumbnails of the videos are missing.\n\n**Regression range**\n* This is not a regression.\n\n**Additional notes**\n* Refreshing the page successfully loads all video thumb nails.\n* After a refresh, the videos are fully loaded each time the user re-visits the AOL videos website.",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "Created attachment 9575428\nThe videos from AOL are only loaded after a refresh.mp4\n\n**Found in**\n* 151.0b3\n\n**Affected versions**\n* Nigthly - 152.0a1 \n* Firefox Beta - 151.0b3\n* Firefox 150.0.1\n* Firefox 140.10.1 ESR\n* Firefox 115.35.1 ESR\n\n**Tested platforms**\n* Affected platforms: macOS 26.4, Windows 11, Ubuntu 24.04\n\n**Preconditions**\n* Run this on a fresh profile\n\n**Steps to reproduce**\n1. Navigate to [AOL videos site.](https://www.aol.com/video/)\n2. Check the displayed videos.\n\n**Expected result**\n* The videos should be fully loaded (thumbnails and title as well).\n\n**Actual result**\n* The thumbnails of the videos are missing.\n\n**Regression range**\n* This is not a regression.\n\n**Additional notes**\n* Refreshing the page successfully loads all video thumb nails.\n* After a refresh, the videos are fully loaded each time the user re-visits the AOL videos website.",
              "time": "2026-04-30T12:11:25Z"
            },
            {
              "attachment_id": null,
              "author": "dholbert@mozilla.com",
              "bug_id": 2036045,
              "count": 1,
              "creation_time": "2026-05-05T16:13:41Z",
              "creator": "dholbert@mozilla.com",
              "id": 18065229,
              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "This only appears to affect the first pageload.\n\nAfter a reload, it fixes itself - I see a bunch of video thumbnail-images as-expected, and Firefox gives me an infobar which lets me know I need to enable DRM video.  If I click the button to enable DRM video, then the videos work properly.\n\nSo something's broken on first pageload, but it gets fixed when some state gets cached or something.",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "This only appears to affect the first pageload.\n\nAfter a reload, it fixes itself - I see a bunch of video thumbnail-images as-expected, and Firefox gives me an infobar which lets me know I need to enable DRM video.  If I click the button to enable DRM video, then the videos work properly.\n\nSo something's broken on first pageload, but it gets fixed when some state gets cached or something.",
              "time": "2026-05-05T16:13:41Z"
            },
            {
              "attachment_id": null,
              "author": "dholbert@mozilla.com",
              "bug_id": 2036045,
              "count": 2,
              "creation_time": "2026-05-05T16:14:28Z",
              "creator": "dholbert@mozilla.com",
              "id": 18065230,
              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "bcaliman, can you confirm that you see the same thing that I describe in comment 1?\n\n(We should still investigate why it's broken on first load and what we can do about that, of course.)",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "bcaliman, can you confirm that you see the same thing that I describe in comment 1?\n\n(We should still investigate why it's broken on first load and what we can do about that, of course.)",
              "time": "2026-05-05T16:14:28Z"
            },
            {
              "attachment_id": null,
              "author": "dholbert@mozilla.com",
              "bug_id": 2036045,
              "count": 3,
              "creation_time": "2026-05-05T17:47:16Z",
              "creator": "dholbert@mozilla.com",
              "id": 18065604,
              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "Oh, sorry, I just read the bug summary (\"are only loaded after a page refresh\") and \"Additional notes\" in comment 0.   I skimmed past those on my first read-through.\n\nIt sounds like you and I are seeing the same behavior indeed.",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "Oh, sorry, I just read the bug summary (\"are only loaded after a page refresh\") and \"Additional notes\" in comment 0.   I skimmed past those on my first read-through.\n\nIt sounds like you and I are seeing the same behavior indeed.",
              "time": "2026-05-05T17:47:16Z"
            },
            {
              "attachment_id": null,
              "author": "dholbert@mozilla.com",
              "bug_id": 2036045,
              "count": 4,
              "creation_time": "2026-05-05T17:57:31Z",
              "creator": "dholbert@mozilla.com",
              "id": 18065621,
              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "I think this may be related to the \"this page needs DRM\" logic/infobar.\n\nNotably:\n- if I perform the STR and then reload the page (and see things in a fixed state) and then I do clear-recent-history (ctrl shift del), the page is **still fixed**.  So the brokenness/fixedness isn't from any sort of  cookie/cache/localstorage/etc.  Though it may be due to some locally-cached state about \"have we already let the user know that this page requires DRM, or kicked off the Widevine plugin download in case the user opts to activate it\".\n- if I start with a brand new fresh profile, and I insert this additional step before the STR...\n[Step 0: Visit some other site that uses DRM video, e.g. https://finance.yahoo.com, and click through the enable-DRM infobar]\n...and then I perform the STR (loading https://www.aol.com/video/ ) , then I get expected results.",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "I think this may be related to the \"this page needs DRM\" logic/infobar.\n\nNotably:\n- if I perform the STR and then reload the page (and see things in a fixed state) and then I do clear-recent-history (ctrl shift del), the page is **still fixed**.  So the brokenness/fixedness isn't from any sort of  cookie/cache/localstorage/etc.  Though it may be due to some locally-cached state about \"have we already let the user know that this page requires DRM, or kicked off the Widevine plugin download in case the user opts to activate it\".\n- if I start with a brand new fresh profile, and I insert this additional step before the STR...\n[Step 0: Visit some other site that uses DRM video, e.g. https://finance.yahoo.com, and click through the enable-DRM infobar]\n...and then I perform the STR (loading https://www.aol.com/video/ ) , then I get expected results.",
              "time": "2026-05-05T17:57:31Z"
            },
            {
              "attachment_id": null,
              "author": "htsai@mozilla.com",
              "bug_id": 2036045,
              "count": 5,
              "creation_time": "2026-05-07T11:02:49Z",
              "creator": "htsai@mozilla.com",
              "id": 18069620,
              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "Enabling dom.script_loader.external_scripts.speculate_link_preload.enabled seems to resolve the issue for me, as what's investigated in bug 2030614",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "Enabling dom.script_loader.external_scripts.speculate_link_preload.enabled seems to resolve the issue for me, as what's investigated in bug 2030614",
